0w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ks573k7u/bb59c1a6-0397-406a-8ddd-19e6fc882f80/911f9eb0-f95f-11eb-896d-4d830e0f8af0/file-1ks573k7v.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2020 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 36 English Explanation 2\"></picture> <br><br>Now we can clearly see, that compound P is same as given compound, thus compound P is identical to D-erythrose.<br><br>Compound Q and D-erythrose are not mirror images of one another and are non-superimposable on one another. Thus, they are diastereomers.<br><br>Compound R and D-erythrose are also not mirror images of one another and are non-superimposable on one another. Thus, they are diastereomers.<br><br>Compound S and D-erythrose are chiral molecules. They are mirror images of one another. Furthermore, the molecules are non-superimposable on one another. This means that the molecules cannot be placed on top of one another and give the same molecule. Chiral molecules with one or more stereocenters can be enantiomers.<br><br>Hence, the correct option is (c)."
